   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 5,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## A shader on the windows\n\n**kubakub shader** draws moving pictures with a small program that runs on the graphics card. Here the preset *scan band* runs two bands of light along the field from **kubakub mask field** (the distance from each window's edge; nothing connected = the windows of the sample facade) and flashes on the beat. No AI model.\n\n**Try:** press **pick a preset by its picture** at the bottom of the node and click another one (clouds, fire, plasma, tunnel, starfield ...). Change the numbers in `controls` (the report lists every control), raise `loops`.\n\n**A shader from shadertoy.com:** open it there, click into the code, Ctrl+A, Ctrl+C, then paste into `code`. You do not need to understand it; the node says what it needs. Connect your own regions to the field and your own sound to `audio`. `images` and `masks` go into any node, or as a layer into the kubakub director."
   ]
  }
 ],
